  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Calm ambient only: mountains and mist for the long stay (no cave or sleepers drawn), then the geometric pattern for Allah's attributes (knowledge of the unseen, seeing, hearing, sole rule). Verse 25 is a 7 s chapter so the mood can change with the meaning. Both tafsirs take verse 25 as Allah's statement of the duration. v2: 26:1-5 (address to the Prophet) is a quiet range; the key plate leaves before His attributes (26:10-12), which get a geometric ring instead of a light swell; a sideways pan replaces the push-in on 26:16. v2b: no sky tilt on His attribute (26:7, a pan instead) and no sparkle on the rosette at 26:18."
